{"author":{"id":"038d65070aa747b6bc9d50939fa697ec871a40ed259db54429b255bbef2581d6"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1793040253,"nonce":"PwoeQ0ZQerbD5QzXTvl+98RR+50=","message":"Completed in 52a60fe.\n\nHosted direct writes now reserve bounded workspace-scoped payload space atomically with the pending filesystem intent, then upload an immutable SHA-256-addressed object to private R2 before forwarding to compute. Existing objects are verified before reuse. Text, binary and empty files are supported. Payloads deduplicate within a workspace and remain available across later overwrite/move/delete. Failed or interrupted uploads remain quota-accounted; upload or verification failures do not reach compute. Storage I/O has a deadline and exports release the recovery gate during object reads, then verify the catalog revision again.\n\nThe private owner/source/revision-checked /recovery/file endpoint exports only applied operations with payload references. It verifies object length and digest and exposes neither a public route nor bucket URL. Pending, uncertain, refused and older payload-less operations fail closed. The catalog and exports keep automaticRestore:false; operation bytes are historical, so a materializer must respect the complete ordered history.\n\nValidation: all 17 Rust Worker integration tests passed. A proxy verifies the durable intent and exact R2 bytes before forwarding the write to native compute. Tests cover binary/Unicode/empty data, same-content dedup, separate-account/workspace storage prefixes and quotas, private route/source/revision enforcement, corrupt/missing/unconfigured storage, interrupted writes, object restart, deletion of all compute files/state, restoring exported bytes on fresh compute, and quota rejection before object upload or native side effects. Full hosted WASM sign-in, repository selection, unsaved edit recovery, durable Save and reload passed. WASM and native session rebuilt; tested bundle staged at bin/web/rayde; existing session restarted with URL/state/credentials preserved and live hello/file-read checks passed.\n\nPrototype payload guards: 12 MiB/file, 64 MiB retained raw bytes and 1,024 distinct payloads/workspace. All retained versions and potential uploads count toward quota. These are separate from document recovery and future paid-tier/Cloud Sync policy. Automatic payload reclamation is not implemented.\n\nReal Cloudflare integration is not required for this local milestone: tests use emulated Durable Objects and R2. Before deployment we need the account, actual private R2 bucket, Worker/auth secrets/domain configuration and a real isolated runner. No resources provisioned, push or deployment. Full filesystem baseline/Git state, external-change reconciliation, saved-versus-dirty restore, stable identities, compute leases/fencing, automated materialization and production MSB provisioning remain under the parent tracks.","files":null}]}